==Portuguese==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|roa-ptg|pt}} {{term|bairro|lang=roa-ptg}}, {{term|barrio|lang=roa-ptg}}, from {{etyl|ar|pt}} {{term|barri|barrī|lang=ar}}, referring to the outer, surrounding or less civilized or urbanized parts of a city. Compare Spanish ''[[barrio]]''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|PT}} {{IPA|/ˈbaj.ʁu/|lang=pt}}
* {{hyphenation|bair|ro}}

